course: dictionary
lesson: 1919
title: Comedy and the funny side
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A comedy is a film, play, show or story meant to make people laugh. The word can also name one funny film or play: «The Greeks invented theatre, with comedies and tragedies performed in great open-air theatres.» Here comedies are the funny plays, and tragedies are the sad ones, so the two words sit as opposites.
explain: Comedy can also mean the funny side of something. «Cartoons and comedy exaggerate politicians on purpose to make people laugh and think.» Exaggerate means to make something seem bigger or more than it really is, so the clue tells you that comedy here means a funny way of showing things.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping in a simpler idea. "Cartoons and funny shows exaggerate politicians on purpose" still makes sense, so comedy means funny shows in that sentence. Look for clues such as "make people laugh" and you will often find the meaning.
explain: In English lessons, comedy is often set against tragedy. Shakespeare's comedies end happily, while a tragedy ends in sadness. The context of a text tells you which one you are reading.
fact: Comedy means films, plays, shows or stories meant to make people laugh.
fact: «Comedy» can also mean the funny side of something, as in the comedy of the situation.
fact: A comedy of errors is a chain of silly mistakes.
fact: «Comedies» are plays with a happy ending, such as Shakespeare's comedies, and they are the opposite of tragedies.
fact: Stand-up comedy is when one person tells jokes to an audience.
exercise: «Memes and comedy can spark curiosity, but you need to know the real story to understand the joke.» What is comedy in this sentence? | A great open-air theatre | *A happy ending in a play | Films, plays, shows or stories meant to make people laugh | A kind of tinned meat
exercise: Shakespeare's comedies end happily. What is a comedy in English literature? | *A play with a happy ending | A sad song | A play with a sad ending | A long poem about kings
exercise: What does «a comedy of errors» mean? | A story about a sad hero | *A chain of silly mistakes | A quiet, gloomy day | A film about a lost map
test: «Cartoons and comedy exaggerate politicians on purpose to make people laugh.» What does exaggerate mean? | Hide something from view | *Make something look bigger or more than it really is | Make something quieter | Repeat something over and over
test: «"Spam" for junk messages comes from a 1970 Monty Python comedy sketch.» In this sentence, what is a comedy sketch? | A long true story about a war | A type of tinned meat only | A map of a city | *A short funny scene meant to make people laugh
exam: Which sentence uses comedy to mean the funny side of something? | The Greeks invented theatre | *The comedy of the situation made everyone giggle | The dog's tail drooped | Shakespeare wrote many plays
